{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00427",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.09,
      "end_seconds": 7.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Yeah, doctor, hello, I've got my papers here, where should I put them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.6,
      "end_seconds": 12.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.17,
      "end_seconds": 16.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.49,
      "end_seconds": 21.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.64,
      "end_seconds": 30.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Honestly, it's burning when I pass urine, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.76,
      "end_seconds": 32.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.28,
      "end_seconds": 42.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.07,
      "end_seconds": 49.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.56,
      "end_seconds": 63.68,
      "duration_seconds": 13.12,
      "text": "A five out of ten, I suppose. It comes and goes. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.45,
      "end_seconds": 72.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "What about an urgent need to pass urine, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.05,
      "end_seconds": 82.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.48,
      "text": "Yes, that started yesterday. Yeah, about urgent need to pass urine, I'd say mild. I've had cloudy, smelly urine too, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.57,
      "end_seconds": 87.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.68,
      "end_seconds": 91.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "No problem, um, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.05,
      "end_seconds": 94.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Okay, and vaginal discharge, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.29,
      "end_seconds": 98.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Yeah, not at all, no vaginal discharge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.16,
      "end_seconds": 104.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "And vomiting, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.54,
      "end_seconds": 107.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "No vomiting, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 107.68,
      "end_seconds": 112.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice vomiting. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.36,
      "end_seconds": 117.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.02,
      "end_seconds": 130.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Let me check a few things. Any fever, similar episode recently or blood in the urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.98,
      "end_seconds": 134.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Nothing like that, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.47,
      "end_seconds": 138.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.3,
      "end_seconds": 141.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.96,
      "end_seconds": 145.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.63,
      "end_seconds": 147.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.75,
      "end_seconds": 159.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.03,
      "end_seconds": 163.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "So, my sister has epilepsy. My grandmother had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.04,
      "end_seconds": 168.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Right, do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.6,
      "end_seconds": 173.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Yeah, I'm allergic to eggs, I get a rash. Yes, aspirin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.84,
      "end_seconds": 177.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.38,
      "end_seconds": 183.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "I mean, yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.53,
      "end_seconds": 187.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.67,
      "end_seconds": 192.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Metformin. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.3,
      "end_seconds": 195.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.28,
      "end_seconds": 202.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Nearly five years now. I'm on apixaban, twice a day for the heart rhythm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.73,
      "end_seconds": 205.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.54,
      "end_seconds": 210.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "5 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.8,
      "end_seconds": 212.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.76,
      "end_seconds": 217.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Yes, I had a C-section, about ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.49,
      "end_seconds": 222.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.91,
      "end_seconds": 223.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.6,
      "end_seconds": 244.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.78,
      "end_seconds": 252.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for about ten years now. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.51,
      "end_seconds": 254.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.88,
      "end_seconds": 256.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Yes, an irregular heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.2,
      "end_seconds": 278.98,
      "duration_seconds": 21.78,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Yes, I can see the an irregular heartbeat in your file as well. What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.51,
      "end_seconds": 282.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 283.4,
      "end_seconds": 289.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse 64, blood pressure 108 over 69, temperature is 36.9 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.64,
      "end_seconds": 290.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.49,
      "end_seconds": 293.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.23,
      "end_seconds": 297.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Of course, uh, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.77,
      "end_seconds": 308.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.07,
      "end_seconds": 313.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.04,
      "end_seconds": 320.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Okay, um, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.39,
      "end_seconds": 322.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.45,
      "end_seconds": 337.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "There's mild tenderness above the pubic bone, and no tenderness in the loins."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.7,
      "end_seconds": 348.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.91,
      "end_seconds": 352.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.12,
      "end_seconds": 353.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.11,
      "end_seconds": 377.05,
      "duration_seconds": 14.94,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is a urinary tract infection. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be a kidney infection, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.11,
      "end_seconds": 380.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.84,
      "end_seconds": 396.22,
      "duration_seconds": 15.38,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a urinary tract infection do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had burning when you pass urine, and no blood in the urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.62,
      "end_seconds": 398.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.61,
      "end_seconds": 412.47,
      "duration_seconds": 13.86,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.77,
      "end_seconds": 414.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.85,
      "end_seconds": 438.83,
      "duration_seconds": 22.98,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a urine test for urinary symptoms. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'm going to order a urine culture, for urinary symptoms. I'd like you to take trimethoprim, 200 milligrams, twice a day, for three days. It's for urine infection. Drink plenty of water and don't hold it in when you need to go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.86,
      "end_seconds": 449.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you get a fever, back pain or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 450.01,
      "end_seconds": 452.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Yes, you know, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.22,
      "end_seconds": 458.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again if it's not better in three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 459.18,
      "end_seconds": 463.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Hmm, sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 464.87,
      "end_seconds": 472.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "Alright, just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 473.53,
      "end_seconds": 483.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.44,
      "text": "So, um, I take the trimethoprim, 200 milligrams, twice a day and come back if it's not better in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 484.28,
      "end_seconds": 488.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "So, yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0074",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 489.44,
      "end_seconds": 492.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Uh, no, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0075",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 494.27,
      "end_seconds": 495.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}